Rule 1 (Input tensor must be 1 or 2 dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 2
>>
Rule 2 (If input tensor is 2D, it can be converted to 1D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 4 (The input tensor's data type should be valid)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12
>>
Rule 5 (If input is 2D, the offset should not be greater than the difference between dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then v_2 ≥ (0 - shape(v_1, 0)) ∧ v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 6 (If input is 1D, the output must be a square matrix)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : true
>>
Rule 7 (If input is 2D, the resulting 1D array's length must be equal to one of the dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then (shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1))
>>
Rule 8 (If offset is non-zero, the result must be padded accordingly.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ v_2 ≠ 0 then true
>>
Rule 10 (The input tensor should have at least one element)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then shape(v_1, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 11 (If the input is 1D, its length must be non-negative.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 12 (If input is 2D, both dimensions must be non-negative.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 18 (The offset value cannot cause out-of-bounds access with 2D inputs.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then (shape(v_1, 0) + v_2) > 0 ∧ (shape(v_1, 1) - v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 19 (If offset is positive with a 2D input, shape[0] should be greater or equal than offset)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2 > 0 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ v_2
>>
Rule 20 (If offset is negative with a 2D input, shape[1] should be greater or equal than the absolute value of offset)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2 < 0 then shape(v_1, 1) ≥ (0 - v_2)
>>
Rule 21 (For 1D input, offset is meaningless)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then v_2 = 0
>>
Rule 22 (If the input is 2D and the offset is zero, the output dimension must match the input dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2 = 0 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 25 (Input Dtype must be numerical. )
